40
00:07:09,631 --> 00:07:12,631
How to summarize a longer text.

41
00:07:12,631 --> 00:07:21,671
Summarizing a text or distilling its essential concepts into a paragraph or two is a useful

42
00:07:21,671 --> 00:07:24,631
study tool as well as good writing practice.

43
00:07:24,631 --> 00:07:32,631
Of course, when you are studying, when you are reading an article, a book, a research paper,

44
00:07:32,631 --> 00:07:37,631
it will help you if you can summarize what you have learned.

45
00:07:37,631 --> 00:07:46,631
You can take notes and summarizing will make it shorter and simpler to revise it later.

46
00:07:46,631 --> 00:08:03,631
It has two aims to reproduce the overarching ideas, very important ideas in a text, identifying the general concepts that run through the entire piece, and to express these overarching ideas using a precise specific language.

47
00:08:03,631 --> 00:08:04,631
Okay.

48
00:08:04,631 --> 00:08:08,631
When you summarize, you cannot rely on the language.

49
00:08:08,631 --> 00:08:09,631
Okay.

50
00:08:09,631 --> 00:08:12,631
I'm not going to read everything line by line.

51
00:08:15,668 --> 00:08:17,888
You can read it, okay, later.

52
00:08:20,228 --> 00:08:27,867
Okay, when you are given a text to summarize in the exam or during your studies,

53
00:08:29,067 --> 00:08:33,368
of course, you need to take a look at the text first, previewing,

54
00:08:33,947 --> 00:08:40,108
looking at the title, subheadings, if there are some pictures, captions,

55
00:08:40,567 --> 00:08:45,427
then you will have an idea about what the text tells you.

56
00:08:45,668 --> 00:08:50,567
What is the aim of the text or the aim of the author?

57
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:52,967
What does it talk about?

58
00:08:54,868 --> 00:09:01,048
And very important point, please, in your first sentence,

59
00:09:01,668 --> 00:09:07,207
write the title of the text and the name of the author, okay?

60
00:09:07,207 --> 00:09:12,148
We will see some examples for that, how you can do it in the first sentence.

61
00:09:12,148 --> 00:09:19,548
But of course, you are free as long as you mention the title of the text.

62
00:09:19,968 --> 00:09:27,927
In the text, X, the writer, Y, tells about this.

63
00:09:28,427 --> 00:09:31,508
Your first sentence must be like this, okay?

64
00:09:31,508 --> 00:09:36,927
The title of the text and the name of the author must be included.

65
00:09:38,567 --> 00:09:46,307
It's like one third of the general points that you will get from the summary, okay?

66
00:09:46,548 --> 00:09:47,728
The first sentence.

67
00:09:48,408 --> 00:09:49,707
It's very important.

68
00:09:49,707 --> 00:09:51,368
Okay.

69
00:09:51,707 --> 00:09:57,228
And this first sentence should contain the author's thesis,

70
00:09:57,768 --> 00:10:01,108
the central concept stated in your own words.

71
00:10:01,327 --> 00:10:04,087
As I told you, you must take a look at the text,

72
00:10:04,207 --> 00:10:07,207
