You need to use quotation marks, normally, when you are writing a report or something.

142
00:15:00,028 --> 00:15:08,028
But in the summary, please don't use quotation marks or don't, as long as it's not a slogan or something.

143
00:15:08,028 --> 00:15:14,028
Of course, if a slogan is taken, okay, you need to take it as it is.

144
00:15:14,028 --> 00:15:22,028
Otherwise, when you are summarizing, you mustn't use the same sentence or even a few words.

145
00:15:22,028 --> 00:15:29,028
If you do use even a few of the author's words, they must appear in quotation marks.

146
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:36,028
To avoid plagiarism, try writing the first draft of your summary without looking back at the original text.

147
00:15:36,028 --> 00:15:37,028
Yes.

148
00:15:37,028 --> 00:15:43,028
You can read the text twice or more, and then you decide.

149
00:15:43,028 --> 00:15:46,028
You can think it like this.

150
